      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The _id value of a stored document is immutable. The official $createObjectId example that supplies a new _id does so in a view's $project, not in an update of stored documents. Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/document.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/createObjectId/",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/document.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3f34205e2489c1607f886fce5e38ef18af0e8560deacbeb07802793cab00acdb",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
